<v Mike>So, I agree, especially because they're leaning into, you know, like, that line about the, you know, do you feel lucky, punk, and all that.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.020
<v Sean>It makes sense. They say it pretty often.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.180
<v Mike>Right, right. It makes sense.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.580
<v Mike>But here's the thing, just to go back to the beginning of the game.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:34.420
<v Mike>I don't want to recap everything I said, but there is some kind of cardinal sin about, like, a level starting immediately.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.920
<v Mike>Like, that's a jank feeling of, like, why am I just being, like, thrown into something that feels like it was already happening?

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:44.800
<v Mike>But why are, like, two enemies literally punching you at the start?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.360
<v Mike>Like, are you waking up from something?

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.320
<v Mike>Are you waking up from the previous game over?

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:54.580
<v Joe>Yeah, it's just, like, this is where, no, this is just, like, where you pick up the story.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:58.240
<v Joe>But, like, moments before was, like, exactly the same part of the story.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.560
<v Joe>They're just like, yeah, we'll start you here.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:07.420
<v Mike>Right, right. You could have just started a couple frames over to the left and just started beating them up instead, but they chose you to be in the middle of them.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:20.280
<v Sean>Yeah, if this was a more modern game, maybe it would start with a cutscene of, like, I don't know, something completely unrelated to Dirty Harry because he never got himself into these situations, like, all willy-nilly.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:23.580
<v Sean>It really is strange.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:35.940
<v Sean>Like, you'd think that, like, if you wanted to at least even add to the fact that maybe this is the character that you remember from in the movies, maybe just have him leave a police station and walk out onto the street.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:44.120
<v Sean>Or is it really that important to immediately say to everyone, like, no, this is an action game.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.660
<v Sean>You're going to have to be really good at this.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.080
<v Sean>I don't know. It felt like a very strange decision.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:53.980
<v Mike>I agree. Getting around in the city, sometimes it's like, where the hell do I go?

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:59.020
<v Mike>But it's because streets are not simple left to right side-scrolling levels.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:06.200
<v Mike>You can not only walk throughout the streets, but you can walk into alleys or through doors to side areas.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:09.140
<v Mike>You can go down into the sewers via the manholes.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.600
<v Mike>It's easy. You can climb power lines.

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:19.760
<v Mike>Right. It's easy to kind of get, like, lost in this larger, like, what's my objective?

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:27.180
<v Mike>You know, like, you're kind of just exploring, but you don't have, like, a quest thing to be like, well, first you should go into this building and do this.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.300
<v Mike>Then you should go into this alleyway.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.640
<v Mike>You kind of just have to figure it all out.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:45.040
<v Mike>So while it is a pretty impressive city to walk around in for NES days, like, compared to, I guess, like, we've had some other ones where it's more, like, top down and you're driving around in a city and then you go to levels.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:59.220
<v Mike>This feels okay, but it's the controls that make it so tough to get around that really, like, limit the amount of exploration you want to do before you're just like, okay, where the hell do I go?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:05.560
<v Joe>Yeah. What's impressive to me about it on paper is that it's not that top down style where you're used to sitting in other games.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:06.760
<v Joe>And it is a side scroller.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.740
<v Joe>It's like a beat them up side scroller, like any other one that we've played.

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:13.320
<v Joe>But you can go into a bunch of the buildings and you can go into all the buildings.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.380
<v Joe>You hear that GTA?

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:21.960
<v Joe>But, like, you can go into all the buildings and you can, like, there is a city, but it's in a side scrolling style.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:26.440
<v Joe>And that is a really cool, like, design idea for me.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.520
<v Joe>And I love that idea for games.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:38.280
<v Joe>I just don't know if, like, each of the parts of this work together or, like, if it just gets kind of frustrating, actually, in practice.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.180
<v Joe>Or maybe it's just the way this game pulled it off.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.460
<v Sean>The controls really are a mystery.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.020
<v Sean>And I think this, I'm going to answer this in two parts.

00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:56.120
<v Sean>I think that the bigger sin here is, at least specifically in this level, is the lack of direction.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:02.360
<v Sean>Because this is kind of, like, a, it's a huge riddle.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.060
<v Sean>You're supposed to, like, progress in this game.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.940
<v Sean>Like, are you supposed to go in the sewers?

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:12.140
<v Sean>Is that, like, the end goal is to get to the bottom of the sewers?

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:17.160
<v Sean>Or is there, like, a, or is there, like, a building you're supposed to gain access to?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:23.980
<v Sean>You end up figuring out that, yes, it's the sewers because you've pressed every other option.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:29.400
<v Sean>And I guess, like, the main progression point there is to get, like, a flashlight.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:39.960
<v Sean>But, yeah, the controls are so strange, though, that I would say that, I know that, Mike, I know you don't like up as jump.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:42.540
<v Sean>I'm okay with up as jump.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:48.620
<v Sean>But even you, I think, can agree that up is better as jump than A and B.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.800
<v Mike>A hundred percent. Yes.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:55.540
<v Joe>You know what? I'm going to play Crazy Devil's Advocate here.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:59.500
<v Sean>I would have agreed with you when I read the manual of this and I saw A and B was jump.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.720
<v Sean>But in practice, in this game, I think I like it better than up.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:07.300
<v Joe>I don't think it's great, but I think up is just more annoying because I can't keep moving forward.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.980
<v Joe>Like, it's just not as fluid to me.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.220
<v Sean>Okay, Joe, then.

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:13.320
<v Sean>But let me just, let me press you there, though.

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:19.480
<v Sean>Okay. Let's say that, like, okay, A and B is jump and you're okay with that.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:23.400
<v Mike>Now, do you think maybe up should be how you interact with people?

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:32.760
<v Sean>Or should it be you jump like a weirdo in front of them and that's how you get any kind of, like, pickup from that person?

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:47.540
<v Sean>Because there's nothing weirder to me than, like, finding that room with the girl that gives you the extra lives past, like, the big dude that's bulletproof than having to, like, jump clear over her head and then land again.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.740
<v Sean>And that's how you, like, get the lives.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:50.760
<v Sean>It's so goofy.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.320
<v Joe>I mean, I don't feel like that's pressing me.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:19:04.800
<v Joe>I mean, I think that those can be, those are not, like, those are, like, very exclusive two different things where, like, I think A and B is better than up for me, but also what you just described is really stupid and I hate it.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:10.900
<v Joe>So, like, I don't want both of those things to be true, but, like, I don't think A and B is ideal.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:14.060
<v Joe>But I just, it just didn't bother me as much as I thought when I read it in the manual.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.220
<v Joe>I was like, well, that's going to be awful.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.500
<v Joe>And then I kind of forgot about it.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:17.520
<v Joe>I got used to it pretty quickly.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:23.500
<v Mike>And even if the control isn't bad, we can agree that the jump itself is just bad.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.780
<v Mike>It's just a bad jump.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:25.840
<v Mike>It's very stiff.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.880
<v Sean>Yeah. He's quite, he can gallop, though.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.160
<v Mike>He's a good jumper.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.500
<v Mike>Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. Great, great jumper from no momentum.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.240
<v Joe>And I assume he does a lot of acrobatics in the movie and stuff and he climbs and jumps.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:41.100
<v Sean>He does jump from a bridge onto a bus in the first movie.

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:42.860
<v Joe>Oh, okay. Then you've got to be a good jumper for that.

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.100
<v Sean>So that might be based on the movie.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.220
<v Mike>We were talking about getting around in the city.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.900
<v Mike>And, you know, I guess in one way they're trying to encourage exploration.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:58.620
<v Mike>But they're really not because that door closes as soon as you enter the ha ha ha room.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.720
<v Mike>Did you guys come across this?

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.620
<v Joe>I heard about it.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.660
<v Joe>Yeah. Thankfully, I didn't come across it.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:12.940
<v Mike>Okay. So this room, when you enter it from the door, you're just in a room where the letters ha ha ha are on the wall.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.920
<v Mike>And you're soft locked.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.380
<v Mike>You have to reset the game.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.820
<v Joe>Yeah. Can I do my essential games vote right now, actually?

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:22.100
<v Mike>How the hell did he get in that room?

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.420
<v Mike>There's no more door?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:25.540
<v Mike>Like, what happened?

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.360
<v Sean>Yeah. It's a one-time use.

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:29.200
<v Sean>There's nothing off screen, you know?

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:32.380
<v Sean>Like, if it's on screen, it says exit.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.460
<v Sean>And in real life, things will say exit in a place that you can see it.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.360
<v Mike>I don't know. Fourth wall joke.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:40.660
<v Sean>I don't understand.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:45.620
<v Joe>Yeah, fourth wall joke that makes you have to reset your game and just start over.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.800
<v Sean>No, it's bad. It's very bad.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.280
<v Sean>I don't know what they were thinking.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:55.040
<v Sean>Why they think that this would be an acceptable way to treat the player.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:57.480
<v Joe>Like, it's actually insulting.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:00.620
<v Joe>And it's, like, far into that first level, too.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:01.800
<v Joe>It's not like...

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:06.120
<v Joe>Like, if you got there, you made some progress that you lost there.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:10.040
<v Mike>I should go back to the jump, though, because the jump is important for two other things.

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:14.320
<v Mike>Jumping on snakes is how you kill them, just like in real life.

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:17.380
<v Mike>That's true. If you want to take care of a snake, just jump on it.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.580
<v Sean>You jump on boxes, you jump on snakes.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.740
<v Mike>Jumping is also how you change clothes.

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:25.700
<v Mike>Yep. Jump. You have to jump on the guy with the white clothes.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:26.960
<v Mike>Specifically in front of Michael Jackson.

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:32.620
<v Mike>Yeah, yeah, yeah. You jump on the guy with the white clothes, Michael Jackson, and then you become Michael Jackson as a result.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:36.940
<v Mike>But it's also, like, how you interact with other people in the game, too.

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:40.100
<v Mike>Like, you just jump in front of them, and there's that woman.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:41.920
<v Sean>Yeah, the girl in the red dress.

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.680
<v Sean>That's how you get lives, I guess.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:22:03.100
<v Sean>Which I'll also, this is, every time you pick up an item by either jumping on a box or kicking a piece of furniture, which, again, I don't remember from the movie as being his main interaction with the environment, but it will just give you the briefest flash of the thing that you supposedly picked up.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:04.940
<v Sean>You're supposed to kind of just understand.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:09.280
<v Sean>Like, sometimes you'll know, oh, that was a crowbar, but then there's just other shapes.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:15.480
<v Mike>I don't know. Yeah, and there's, like, there aren't all bad ideas.

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:23.100
<v Mike>Like, I feel like we're talking a lot about the funny things, but, like, there was that interesting bodyguard thing, even though they won't tell you in the game what you need to do.

00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:35.060
<v Mike>He's, like, the bouncer who will attack you, and you can't attack him if you're trying to get through the door until you change suits, and then it's like, oh, right this way, come through.

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.080
<v Mike>I'm not saying that's genius, right?

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:46.140
<v Mike>But, like, that is at least, like, they have the idea of gating progress besides just being, like, the door's locked.

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:50.960
<v Mike>Go find the key. I did not realize that it was my clothes that made that happen.

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:55.300
<v Sean>I thought that I just, I thought I jumped past him in the right way.

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:01.560
<v Sean>But I guess I had the suit on at that point, and I just, I tricked myself.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:06.960
<v Mike>Before we move on, one other thing about just the controls and Harry.

00:23:07.260 --> 00:23:11.260
<v Mike>So, he's able to draw the gun, but not shoot it.

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:13.500
<v Mike>And that, we talked about how that looks cool and all.

00:23:14.140 --> 00:23:25.620
<v Mike>Shouldn't he have been able to, like, shouldn't there have been, like, something where he can threaten, or the enemies could feel threatened by just him drawing the gun and kind of, like, nope out of the situation?

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.240
<v Mike>Like, wouldn't that have been interesting?

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.480
<v Mike>That would have been more Dirty Harry.

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:30.720
<v Mike>Dirty Harry? Right, you know?

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.960
<v Mike>Like, he's more, like, in your face.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:34.800
<v Mike>Like, is this guy really going to shoot me?

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:35.720
<v Mike>He's a cop.

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:37.880
<v Mike>He shouldn't shoot me, but he looks kind of crazy.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:38.720
<v Mike>Maybe he will.

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:40.320
<v Mike>But they don't give a shit.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:41.960
<v Mike>Like, they're just, like, coming at you.

00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:49.220
<v Joe>Yeah, I mean, was this game, I mean, not to get ahead of whatever, like, developer notes, but was this game designed to be a Dirty Harry game?

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:52.100
<v Joe>Or was this just a game that didn't have anything to do with Dirty Harry?

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:54.380
<v Sean>I think that it definitely was.

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:55.800
<v Sean>It had to have been.

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:59.000
<v Sean>There's too many, like, just Clint Eastwood references and everything.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.420
<v Joe>Well, yeah, but I mean, like, originally, like, you know, they just slapped that stuff in at the end after they were like, all right, yeah, let's just make it Clint Eastwood.

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:11.500
<v Mike>Let's make it. To the best of my knowledge, this was always a Dirty Harry game.

00:24:12.220 --> 00:24:13.520
<v Joe>Well, then, weird decisions.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:20.460
<v Mike>Yeah. Weird decisions all around because, keep in mind, the Dirty Harry series ended in 1988.

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:27.460
<v Mike>So it's not, like, it's not gone, like, real old news or whatever, but there's not, like, in promotion of some new movie.

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:36.080
<v Joe>Yeah, but all things considered, it's this being, like, ending in 1988 is, like, that's, like, pretty good compared to, like, half the other games.

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:37.600
<v Joe>Like, that's just happening right now.

00:24:37.720 --> 00:24:41.260
<v Joe>Like, we've had games that were, like, from properties from, like, the 60s only.

00:24:41.260 --> 00:24:43.580
<v Sean>Yeah, this isn't, like, three stooges in Jaws.

00:24:43.620 --> 00:24:49.260
<v Sean>Like, this is much more in vogue than I expected it to be.

00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:53.020
<v Sean>I didn't realize that it was up to 1988, actually.

00:24:53.020 --> 00:24:53.880
<v Sean>That's pretty recent.

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:57.280
<v Mike>Yeah, you think about 71 to 88, but it's five films.

00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:59.580
<v Mike>So it's, like, they really knew how to draw them out back then.

00:25:01.920 --> 00:25:07.200
<v Mike>And going through, probably, like, I'm just going to skip through, like, most of the rest of this game.

00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:10.600
<v Mike>Harry's arsenal expands.

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:12.880
<v Mike>Obviously, we get more enemies and everything.

00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:14.840
<v Mike>We go to two different stages.

00:25:14.840 --> 00:25:20.060
<v Mike>We have the docks, and we have Alcatraz Island as our final stages.

00:25:20.220 --> 00:25:23.000
<v Mike>So there's only three stages, and the game does make that clear.

00:25:23.220 --> 00:25:25.940
<v Mike>They just don't make it clear, like, how big those things are.

00:25:26.020 --> 00:25:28.460
<v Mike>They make it seem like it's just level one, level two, level three.

00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:30.760
<v Mike>But they ask you for that when you start the game.

00:25:30.940 --> 00:25:34.200
<v Mike>Do you want to, like, do you put in a password for level two or three?

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:35.900
<v Mike>And you're kind of like, only three levels?

00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:37.020
<v Mike>Like, that's kind of interesting.

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:39.780
<v Sean>Level one is pretty huge, though.

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:46.280
<v Sean>But, like, you think that with the whole sort of, I guess, the big city.

00:25:46.480 --> 00:25:49.260
<v Joe>Like, the big, like, complex city arrangement.

00:25:49.260 --> 00:25:51.100
<v Sean>You expect that to be the norm.

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:53.500
<v Sean>And it really isn't that.

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:57.480
<v Sean>Like, the city is only, like, half of level one.

00:25:57.480 --> 00:26:06.240
<v Sean>And then the other, I want to say, like, 55% of it is in the sewers, which is much less fun and much less interesting.

00:26:06.540 --> 00:26:13.260
<v Sean>I mean, not to say that the city was perfect execution on everything.

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:18.360
<v Sean>But at least, like, it felt more like an interesting environment to explore.

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:21.680
<v Sean>Whereas the sewers are just, you know, another video game sewer.

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:28.660
<v Mike>I don't know. But does it ever feel like the stakes are getting larger as the game goes on?

00:26:28.660 --> 00:26:32.960
<v Mike>As you're taking down this larger super gang that we discussed?

00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:36.820
<v Mike>You do have access to some pretty cool stuff as the game goes on.

00:26:37.020 --> 00:26:39.500
<v Mike>You get the, there's rockets.

00:26:39.500 --> 00:26:40.600
<v Mike>There's a harpoon.

00:26:42.680 --> 00:26:44.220
<v Mike>And the RC cars.

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:48.220
<v Joe>Yes, the RC cars.

00:26:48.220 --> 00:26:49.180
<v Joe>No better way to raise the stakes.

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:51.860
<v Mike>Yeah. The RC explosive cars, keep in mind.

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:53.440
<v Mike>It's like, did he go to queue for those?

00:26:53.560 --> 00:27:00.940
<v Mike>Like, what's happening? Health, though, is refilled by eating hot dogs that you find on the streets.

00:27:00.940 --> 00:27:06.980
<v Mike>And I hope nobody, and I mean nobody, put ketchup on those hot dogs.

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:10.480
<v Mike>Okay. Is this, are you trying to make a statement right now?

00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:14.080
<v Mike>Like, it's a reference from the film.

